  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 30-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Initialize layer thicknesses from the Round 1 best candidate thicknesses [59.0, 95.0, 64.0, 91.0, 100.0, 131.0, 57.0, 98.0, 96.0, 91.0, 61.0, 90.0, 56.0, 77.0, 55.0, 71.0, 51.0, 86.0, 99.0, 93.0, 78.0, 127.0, 77.0, 71.0, 42.0, 52.0, 73.0, 87.0, 49.0, 115.0] nm with ±5% multiplicative perturbation applied to each layer. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with maximum step size 0.5 nm per iteration. Evaluate spectral performance across 400-700 nm (target: high reflection) and 1530-1565 nm (target: high transmission). Total layer count fixed at 30. Materials: HfO2 (high index), SiO2 (low index), fused silica substrate. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1530–1565 nm; high reflection in 400–700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1530–1565 nm; transmission in 400–700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 30.",
